On 12/05/2016 01:38 AM, Selvin Xavier wrote:
> This patch introduces all the structures used by driver for communicating
> with the Hardware. This file is the equivalent of the bnxt_en_hsi.h used by
> bnxt_en driver.

There are a fair number of structures that are the same between this
file and drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/bnxt/bnxt_hsi.h, for example:

bnxt_re_hsi.h          vs.     bnxt_hsi.h
struct ctx_hw_stats            struct ctx_hw_stats
struct hwrm_async_event_cmpl   struct hwrm_async_event_cmpl
struct cmd_nums
...

Does it make sense to have these two drivers reuse the sections that are
common?
